Sales Performance Analysis
Scope
Sales performance was evaluated across:
The full historical period
Individual stores
Individual departments
Weekly periods
Monthly and quarterly periods
Key Findings
The dataset contains more than $6.74B in sales across 45 stores and 81 departments.
Sales contribution varies materially across stores and departments. This concentration is relevant for resource allocation because changes in high-contribution areas can have a larger effect on overall sales performance.
Business Implications
Store and department performance analysis can support:
- Inventory prioritization
- Store-level planning
- Department-level targets
- Workforce allocation
- Promotional planning
